id: pm-ado-lmey
title: Install the pinned release npm into a job-local prefix
description: "The release workflow replaces the runner's global npm with the pinned npm. Parallel jobs on one runner host share the toolcache Node installation, so one job's global install mutates a sibling job's npm mid-install (ENOTEMPTY, or npm: command not found), as reported by unbraind/pm-ops#284 for the fleet."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-ops#284"
created_at: "2026-11-16T14:41:52.475Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-16T16:07:40.751Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: pi-glm
acceptance_criteria: The release workflow installs the pinned npm with --prefix into a job-local directory and prepends that prefix bin to the job path; The workflow keeps the exact-version assertion on the effective npm; A workflow-contract test fails if any workflow replaces the global npm
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T15:17:20.034Z",codex-sol,"Continuation: verified the existing worktree and remote branch state, preserved the earlier changes, and reused this item. Rerunning required gates to completion under the continuation author before committing results."
  "2026-11-16T15:27:41.370Z",codex-sol,"Root cause confirmed in the workflow source: global installation of the pinned npm replaces the same Node installation used by parallel jobs on a shared toolcache. Replaced each bootstrap with a job-local prefix, published only its bin directory to the job PATH, and retained exact-pin checks including a separate subsequent-step assertion. Workflow contracts reject global npm replacement across all workflow files. No runner settings or shared tool installations were modified."
  "2026-11-16T15:32:08.555Z",codex-sol,"Validation note: this package defines no lint script. Its existing docstring static gate is being run with typecheck, the quick npm test tier, the release workflow contracts and changelog:check; no new lint policy or dependency is introduced for this CI fix."
  "2026-11-16T15:42:12.914Z",codex-sol,The first combined gate command hit its 20-minute timeout during shared-host disk contention and is not pass evidence. Retrying all gates to completion using memory-backed temporary fixtures and the existing harness deadline scale. Assertions and test selection are unchanged.
  "2026-11-16T15:50:16.961Z",codex-sol,"The provenance failures observed during the disk-contention attempt were rechecked separately without source changes: node --test test/closeout-provenance.test.ts completed with all 8 tests passed, no skips or cancellations, using memory-backed temporary fixtures. The complete package gate rerun remains separate evidence."
  "2026-11-16T16:07:40.748Z",codex-sol,"Typecheck and the existing docstring static gate passed; this package has no lint script. Focused workflow tests passed 19 of 20, with the unrelated nested preload acceptance timing out under disk contention. The separate provenance recheck passed all 8 tests. Broad quick gates are active; the preload case will be rechecked from an isolated temporary checkout."
